GUIDES = [
("layered-neutral-bed","How to Layer a Neutral Bed","Bedroom",None,"room:19","The five-layer formula behind every bed that looks styled, not just made.",
"""<p>A neutral bed only looks expensive when it has depth. One color, many textures. Build it in this order and it works every time.</p>
<h2>The five layers</h2><ol><li><b>Crisp base.</b> White or ivory sheets in percale or washed cotton.</li><li><b>Duvet or coverlet.</b> Lightweight, in soft white or oatmeal.</li><li><b>Folded quilt.</b> A third of the way down the bed, a shade darker.</li><li><b>Throw.</b> Something chunky or nubby, tossed near the foot.</li><li><b>Pillows.</b> Two sleeping pillows, two euro shams, one lumbar.</li></ol>
<h2>Why it works</h2><p>Every layer adds a different texture: smooth, matte, quilted, knit, woven. That contrast reads as "designer," even when every piece is a shade of cream.</p>
<h2>The finishing touch</h2><p>Leave it a little imperfect. Plump the pillows, then press a hand into the center of each one. Lived-in beats stiff.</p>""",
["B0CFYFCZ76","B0DKSZYQ5F","B0G255NLXB","B0GQR4HYHR","B0GGR888HN","B0GR4PYCW7","B08GL2W6WY"],19),
("art-above-sofa","How High to Hang Art Above a Sofa","Living Room",None,"room:12","The measurement that fixes most living rooms.",
"""<p>Most art is hung too high. The fix is a single number.</p><h2>The rule</h2><p>Leave <b>8 to 10 inches</b> between the top of the sofa back and the bottom of the frame.</p><h2>How wide</h2><p>Aim for art or a grouping that spans about <b>two-thirds</b> of the sofa's width. One large piece, a pair, or a grid of four all work.</p><h2>For a gallery grid</h2><p>Keep 2 to 3 inches between frames and treat the whole group as one piece when you measure.</p><h2>Check it first</h2><p>Tape paper templates to the wall and live with them for a day before you put in a nail.</p>""",
["B07GSBW1RK","B0FYV1Q29S","B0GWJ5RPG9","B0GRGN77MV","B0DJQGG3XS","B0C2P87NY8"],12),
("rug-size-guide","The Rug Size Guide","Living Room",None,"room:5","Why your rug feels small, and the size that fixes it.",
"""<p>A too-small rug makes a whole room feel off. When in doubt, size up.</p><h2>Living room</h2><p>At least the front legs of every seat should sit on the rug. For most rooms that means 8x10 or larger.</p><h2>Dining room</h2><p>Add about 24 inches past the table on every side so chairs stay on the rug when pulled out.</p><h2>Bedroom</h2><p>The rug should extend 18 to 24 inches past each side of the bed.</p>""",
["B0C4C3VPPL","B0CW4CYY2C","B003X5IC6S","B0CJG2XLTS"],5),
("coffee-table-formula","The Coffee Table Formula","Living Room",None,"room:13","Something tall, something low, something living.",
"""<p>Styling a coffee table is easier with a formula.</p><h2>The three groupings</h2><ol><li><b>Tall:</b> a vase or candlestick.</li><li><b>Low:</b> a stack of two or three books with a small object on top.</li><li><b>Living:</b> branches, a plant or a bowl of fruit.</li></ol><h2>Leave room</h2><p>Keep about a third of the surface open. A coffee table still needs to hold coffee.</p>""",
["B0D27JBMXJ","B0G5842TW7","B0FCFQHDD8","B0GWJHM54G","B0GN27H1WW"],0),
("nightstand-styling","How to Style a Nightstand","Bedroom",None,"room:6","Light, a little lift and one personal thing.",
"""<p>A nightstand needs to be useful first. Then it can be pretty.</p><h2>The essentials</h2><ul><li>A lamp tall enough that the shade sits around shoulder height when you're sitting up in bed.</li><li>A small stack of books for lift.</li><li>One personal item: a small vase, a framed photo or a candle.</li></ul><h2>Hide the rest</h2><p>Choose a nightstand with a drawer so chargers and lotion stay out of sight.</p>""",
["B0CLYVJTDL","B0BS75H57L","B0G5842TW7"],6),
("throw-pillow-formula","The Throw Pillow Formula","Living Room",None,"room:4","Three textures, two sizes, one lumbar.",
"""<p>Pillows are the fastest way to make a sofa look finished, and the easiest place to overdo it.</p><h2>The formula for a sofa</h2><ol><li><b>Two 22-inch squares</b> in a solid or subtle pattern at each end.</li><li><b>Two 20-inch squares</b> in a second texture in front of them.</li><li><b>One lumbar</b> in the middle to tie it together.</li></ol><h2>Mix textures, not colors</h2><p>Stay in one color family and vary the surface: linen, boucle, faux fur, a woven stripe. It reads layered without looking busy.</p><h2>Go down-filled if you can</h2><p>Use inserts 2 inches larger than the cover. That's what makes the classic "chop" hold its shape.</p>""",
["B0DJDMDWCR","B0CSPVLDKB","B0DMXXTWLS","B0DT6V6F33","B0GDF6Y7QZ"],4),
("dining-chandelier-size","How to Size a Dining Chandelier","Dining",None,"room:10","The two numbers that make a chandelier look right.",
"""<p>A chandelier that's too small is the most common dining room miss.</p><h2>Width</h2><p>Aim for a fixture about <b>half to two-thirds the width of the table</b>. For long tables, consider two smaller fixtures.</p><h2>Height</h2><p>Hang the bottom of the fixture <b>30 to 36 inches above the tabletop</b>.</p><h2>Shortcut</h2><p>No table yet? Add the room's length and width in feet. The total, in inches, is a good fixture diameter.</p>""",
["B0CLSY54SD","B0D7ZWDTJG","B0BFVHZRSF","B0F1FJSXHM"],10),
("sideboard-styling","How to Style a Sideboard","Dining",None,"room:16","Anchor, height and something living.",
"""<p>A sideboard is a stage. Give it a backdrop and a little rhythm.</p><h2>The formula</h2><ol><li><b>Anchor:</b> a round mirror or a large piece of art, centered.</li><li><b>Height:</b> a tall vase or candleholder off to one side.</li><li><b>Living:</b> branches or greenery to soften the edges.</li><li><b>Balance:</b> a smaller grouping on the opposite side.</li></ol><h2>Keep it asymmetrical</h2><p>Perfect symmetry looks staged. Let one side be taller than the other.</p><h2>For the holidays</h2><p>Keep the same formula and swap in seasonal layers.</p><ul><li><b>Keep one statement piece:</b> a winter landscape or a mirror still anchors the center.</li><li><b>Run garland along the top:</b> fresh or faux cedar connects the groupings and softens the edges.</li><li><b>Vary the heights:</b> tall winter branches on one side, candlesticks in two or three heights, a stack of books to lift something small.</li><li><b>Group in odd numbers:</b> three candlesticks or a trio of small objects reads more relaxed than pairs.</li><li><b>Add something real:</b> a footed bowl of clementines or pinecones brings color and scent.</li></ul><p>Keep candles away from garland and dry branches, or use flameless tapers.</p>""",
["B0FSKL5257","B0FPF2FQV4","B0GWJHM54G","B0DM9NFVRK"],16),
("entryway-drop-zone","The Entryway Drop Zone","Entryway",None,"img:entryway-drop-zone","A landing spot that looks good and actually gets used.",
"""<p>A great entry does three jobs: somewhere to sit, somewhere to drop and somewhere to hang.</p><h2>The formula</h2><ol><li>A bench for shoes.</li><li>Hooks at two heights, low ones for kids.</li><li>One basket per person.</li><li>A tray for keys.</li></ol><h2>Keep it clear</h2><p>Give each item one home. If it doesn't fit in the basket or the tray, it moves on. A mirror above is the finishing touch.</p>""",
["B0FMF1XJ5G","B0D78P6XCG","B0FCFQHDD8","B0H6LVKTR4"],None),
# Holiday
("thanksgiving-table","A Warm, Simple Thanksgiving Table","Holiday","thanksgiving","room:9","Linen, candlelight and fall branches down the center.",
"""<p>A memorable table is mostly about light and texture, not a centerpiece you can't see over.</p><h2>The recipe</h2><ul><li>A linen runner or tablecloth in a warm neutral.</li><li>Fall branches or greenery laid low down the center.</li><li>Candles under glass at a few heights.</li><li>Woven placemats, fringe napkins and simple napkin rings.</li></ul><h2>The rule of low</h2><p>Keep everything in the center below eye level so guests can talk across the table.</p>""",
["B0H39M1Y7L","B0GB8FFQJY","B0DCB8L72X","B09B73DL7Q","B0GGB6FWR2","B0D1LP2K5Z","B0FSKL5257","B0C5RK3BD5","B0DNLRK1Y6","B09GV787WM","B0G6Z4KK8H","B0DM9NFVRK","B0CSSVRCWK"],9),
("winter-mantel","The Winter Mantel","Holiday","christmas","img:neutral-winter-mantel","One big piece, odd numbers and natural texture.",
"""<p>A mantel looks designed when it has one clear anchor and a few supporting pieces.</p><h2>The formula</h2><ol><li><b>One big piece:</b> a landscape painting or mirror, leaning or hung.</li><li><b>Odd numbers:</b> groups of three or five candlesticks and vases.</li><li><b>Natural texture:</b> branches, greenery or a basket of logs.</li></ol><h2>Keep it calm</h2><p>Stay in a tight palette of cream, wood and green so the room still feels quiet after the holidays.</p><h2>The winter mantel formula</h2><p>Four things, and it works from December through February: <b>art</b> (one large painting, leaning or hung), <b>greenery</b> (a loose, asymmetric cedar or eucalyptus garland draped down one side), <b>brass</b> (two or three candlesticks at different heights) and <b>one natural texture</b> (bare branches in a stoneware vase, old books or a basket of birch logs). After Christmas, take the ornaments off and leave everything else.</p><p>Keep greenery, ribbon and anything flammable well away from the firebox when the fireplace is in use, and use flameless candles near real greenery.</p>""",
["B0FCFQHDD8","B0DM9NFVRK","B0GWJHM54G","B0GRNDLFKZ","B0GSZPQFHH","B0DSW7XDT9","B0DPC5KD18","B0D8HSSLZH","B0BCKSFQWK","B08ZCZXFRB"],None),
("designer-christmas-tree","Why Does Your Tree Look Flat?","Holiday","christmas","img:designer-christmas-tree","Tuck lights deep, add ribbon and use three ornament sizes.",
"""<p>The difference between a pretty tree and a designer tree is depth.</p><h2>Lights first</h2><p>Wrap lights deep inside along the branches, not just around the outside. Aim for about 100 lights per foot of tree.</p><h2>Ribbon next</h2><p>Tuck wide ribbon in loose cascades from top to bottom.</p><h2>Ornaments in three sizes</h2><p>Hang large ornaments deep inside, medium in the middle and small on the tips. It reads as fullness.</p>""",
["B0H8J573ZN","B0D76DXNM9","B09CMDR2D6","B0GZNYDS7D","B0D4Q1J7PP"],None),
("tree-base-styling","Is Your Tree Missing This?","Holiday","christmas","img:tree-base-styling","A woven collar hides the stand and finishes the look.",
"""<p>The tree stand is the one thing that makes a beautiful tree look unfinished.</p><h2>The fix</h2><p>A woven collar or a large basket hides the stand and grounds the tree. Choose one wide enough to cover the stand with a few inches to spare.</p><h2>Then layer</h2><p>Add a chunky throw or a few wrapped gifts in kraft paper and ribbon around the base.</p>""",
["B0H8J573ZN","B0D76DXNM9","B09CMDR2D6","B0GZNYDS7D","B0D4Q1J7PP"],None),
("cozy-christmas-bedroom","Flannel Season: A Cozy Christmas Bedroom","Holiday","christmas","img:cozy-christmas-bedroom","Swap the sheets and add a small wreath.",
"""<p>The bedroom is the easiest room to make feel like the holidays.</p><h2>The swap</h2><ul><li>Plaid or flannel pillow covers on the shams.</li><li>A chunky knit throw at the foot of the bed.</li><li>A small wreath above the headboard.</li><li>Warm lamp light instead of overheads.</li><li>A 2 ft prelit tree on the nightstand.</li><li>Mini wreaths tied to the headboard posts.</li></ul><p>More ideas: <a href=\"/guides/christmas-tree-color-ideas/\">Christmas tree color ideas</a>.</p>""",
["B0D14S1RNR","B0G255NLXB","B0CFYFCZ76","B0CLYVJTDL","B0H3DZV4RP","B07YXTZ33Z","B0CF173VLZ","B0HH8Y296B","B0GVY28QZS","B0HDD74GFM"],None),
("christmas-eve-living-room","Tree Lights On, Overheads Off","Holiday","christmas","img:christmas-eve-living-room","That is the whole secret to a cozy Christmas living room.",
"""<p>The coziest holiday rooms are lit low.</p><h2>Layer the light</h2><ul><li>Tree lights and garland lights on.</li><li>Table lamps on.</li><li>Candles under glass on the coffee table.</li><li>Overheads off.</li></ul><h2>Then add softness</h2><p>A throw on every seat and a few holiday pillow covers make the room feel ready for company.</p>""",
["B0D14S1RNR","B0GGB6FWR2","B0HBBVZDM2","B0HBBVWCVG","B0HBC2BM37","B0HBC6NN18"],None),
("christmas-morning-table","Christmas Morning: Set It the Night Before","Holiday","christmas","img:christmas-breakfast-table","A breakfast table that feels special with almost no work.",
"""<p>Set the table on Christmas Eve and the morning takes care of itself.</p><h2>The setup</h2><ul><li>A linen runner and woven placemats.</li><li>Plaid or fringe napkins with simple rings.</li><li>Greenery in a jar or a low vase.</li><li>A hurricane candle in the center.</li></ul>""",
["B0GB8FFQJY","B0DCB8L72X","B0GJJJC3BP","B0B6G99NZV","B0D8JG8T7R","B0CH9Z8DXC","B0DRBMWKM4"],None),
("cocoa-corner","The Cocoa Corner","Holiday","christmas","img:coffee-cocoa-station","One tray, mugs within reach and toppings in jars.",
"""<p>A cocoa station turns a corner of the counter into a holiday moment.</p><h2>The formula</h2><ol><li>One tray to corral everything.</li><li>Mugs within reach.</li><li>Toppings in clear jars: marshmallows, peppermint, cinnamon sticks.</li><li>A little greenery to soften it.</li></ol>""",
["B0F42DJ5RD","B0GR6BC7VZ","B01F53TT8A","B01EIJ0P6W","B0B28VPQCY","B00266UIP8","B0F8Q4KKZG"],None),
('christmas-coffee-table-decor', 'Christmas Coffee Table Decor Ideas', 'Holiday', 'christmas', 'img:christmas-coffee-table-decor', 'One big tray, one low garland, three candles and a stack of books. Seven pieces, numbered.', '<p>The Christmas coffee tables that look expensive all follow the same rule: one large tray holds everything, and nothing is taller than a candle. People sit around this table, so keep it low enough to talk over and clear enough to set down a mug.</p>\n<h2>The 7 pieces, in order</h2><ol>\n<li><b>A big round wood tray.</b> At 17.7 inches it fills the middle of a standard 48 inch coffee table. Everything else sits on it or right beside it.</li>\n<li><b>A 6 ft real touch cedar garland.</b> Lay it loosely along the back edge or coil it around the tray. Faux cedar looks real at arm\'s length, which matters on a table people sit next to.</li>\n<li><b>Three brass taper holders.</b> Different heights read as styled, not lined up. Put them on the tray.</li>\n<li><b>White taper candles.</b> Unscented and dripless, so they will not compete with dinner.</li>\n<li><b>A pine candle ring.</b> Drop one around a pillar candle for the only bit of red on the table.</li>\n<li><b>Two neutral decorative books.</b> Stack them off center and set something small on top.</li>\n<li><b>Bottle brush trees.</b> A cluster of three in different heights next to the books is the playful moment.</li></ol>\n<h2>The styling rules</h2><ul><li>Keep everything under 12 inches tall so faces stay visible across the table.</li><li>Group in odd numbers: three candles, three trees.</li><li>Leave a third of the table empty for drinks and feet.</li><li>One accent color only. Here it is the red berries in the candle ring.</li></ul>\n<p>Need the everyday version for January? See <a href="/guides/coffee-table-formula/">The Coffee Table Formula</a>. For the whole room, read <a href="/guides/christmas-eve-living-room/">Tree Lights On, Overheads Off</a>.</p>', ['B0CBB3D84J', 'B0H9RWQ9WK', 'B07W554ZNB', 'B07DWH5J2S', 'B0D5BJ3JTR', 'B0DZX91Q4H', 'B08DP4BKGX'], None),
('christmas-entryway-table-decor', 'Christmas Entryway Table Decor', 'Holiday', 'christmas', 'img:christmas-entryway-table-decor', 'A wreath on the mirror, two lamps and one tall vase of pine. The first thing guests see.', '<p>The entry console is the first impression of your whole house at Christmas. The formula is simple: symmetry on the outside, one tall moment off center, and a wreath that hangs on the mirror instead of the door.</p>\n<h2>The 7 pieces, in order</h2><ol>\n<li><b>A round gold mirror</b> centered over the console. It bounces light into a dark entry.</li>\n<li><b>A 20 inch Norfolk cedar wreath</b> hung on the mirror. Twenty inches covers about half a 30 inch mirror, which is the right ratio.</li>\n<li><b>Burgundy velvet ribbon</b> to hang the wreath. Loop it over the top of the mirror and leave long tails.</li>\n<li><b>A pair of marble-base buffet lamps,</b> one at each end. Matching lamps are what make a console look finished.</li>\n<li><b>A large rustic ceramic vase</b> set off center, between the mirror and one lamp.</li>\n<li><b>36 inch Norfolk pine branches</b> in the vase. Tall stems give height without a tree.</li>\n<li><b>Vintage gold bells on jute</b> tied around the neck of the vase.</li></ol>\n<h2>The four-layer Christmas console formula</h2><p>No room for seven pieces? Use four layers: <b>light</b> (one lamp, or a pair), <b>greenery</b> (a low cedar or pine garland running along the top), <b>something gold</b> (a brass bowl of clementines, a small brass reindeer or candlesticks) and <b>one thing to hold the gifts</b> (a woven basket underneath with wrapped presents). A round mirror above pulls it together.</p><h2>The styling rules</h2><ul><li>Lamps first, then the mirror, then the one tall arrangement.</li><li>Keep the middle of the console clear for keys and mail.</li><li>Turn the lamps on at dusk. Lamp light is what makes an entry feel like Christmas.</li></ul>\n<h2>Starting from an empty wall? The whole entry for about $200</h2><p>No console yet? These five pieces build the whole look from scratch for about $200 together (as of November 2026). They are separate picks from the photo above.</p><ol>\n<li><b>A 47 inch fluted console table with drawers.</b> The fluting reads high end, and the drawers hide keys and mail.</li>\n<li><b>A 24 inch gold round mirror</b> centered above it.</li>\n<li><b>A small ceramic table lamp</b> on one end. Light first, always.</li>\n<li><b>A 6 foot real touch cedar garland</b> draped along the top.</li>\n<li><b>A water hyacinth basket</b> on the lower shelf for gifts or shoes.</li></ol>\n<p>Need storage too? See <a href="/guides/entryway-drop-zone/">The Entryway Drop Zone</a>.</p>', ['B0FPF2FQV4', 'B0FM1TLG14', 'B0FH4XMG94', 'B0DN21MGZK', 'B0FJCQHK5B', 'B0FGNHZW9C', 'B0CFT7H56L', 'B0DQ82R8TL', 'B0FWRRTYPT', 'B0GSW26S7M', 'B0FN8BCG3R', 'B0GK6KC6YF'], None),
('kitchen-christmas-decor-ideas', 'Kitchen Christmas Decor Ideas', 'Holiday', 'christmas', 'img:kitchen-christmas-decor-ideas', 'Mini wreaths on the cabinets, red striped towels and one bowl of ornaments. The kitchen is done.', '<p>The kitchen is where everyone ends up at a Christmas party, and it is the easiest room to decorate because the cabinets do the work. Hang small wreaths, swap the towels and add one bowl on the counter.</p>\n<h2>The 6 pieces, in order</h2><ol>\n<li><b>Mini cabinet wreaths, set of 6.</b> Hang them on the upper doors with ribbon over the top of the door. No nails.</li>\n<li><b>Red and white striped KitchenAid towels.</b> Hang one on the oven handle and one on the dishwasher.</li>\n<li><b>A Christmas tree wood serving board</b> left out on the counter with cheese and rosemary.</li>\n<li><b>A white footed pedestal bowl</b> as the counter centerpiece.</li>\n<li><b>Red ball ornaments</b> to fill the bowl.</li>\n<li><b>Norfolk pine branches</b> in a crock by the stove.</li></ol>\n<h2>The styling rules</h2><ul><li>Wreaths on every other door if you have a lot of cabinets.</li><li>Keep the counters 80 percent clear so you can still cook.</li><li>Stick to red, white and green so it reads classic, not cluttered.</li></ul>\n<p>Want a cocoa station next? See <a href="/guides/cocoa-corner/">The Cocoa Corner</a>.</p>', ['B0HDD74GFM', 'B088ZKRQXR', 'B0BCQRGPV3', 'B0DLKKZDB1', 'B0D7PXBM77', 'B0FGNHZW9C'], None),
('christmas-tree-color-ideas', 'Christmas Tree Color Ideas: 3 Formulas That Always Work', 'Holiday', 'christmas', 'img:christmas-tree-brown-and-gold', 'Brown and gold, blue and ivory, or ribbon as the garland. Pick one and buy only those pieces.', '<p>A tree looks designer when it sticks to two colors and one texture. Here are three coordinated two-color approaches, each with its short shopping list. All three sit in the same woven tree collar.</p>\n<h2>Formula 1: Brown and gold</h2><p>Warm, quiet and grown up.</p><ol>\n<li><b>4 inch brown velvet ribbon</b> in loose vertical cascades from the top down.</li>\n<li><b>Champagne mercury glass ornaments</b> tucked deep into the branches.</li>\n<li><b>Neutral velvet bows</b> clipped in the gaps.</li></ol>\n<h2>Formula 2: Blue and ivory</h2><p>Soft, collected and a little unexpected, with gold to keep it warm.</p><p><img src="/images/christmas-tree-blue-and-ivory.jpg" alt="Christmas tree decorated with dusty blue velvet bows, blue and ivory floral ribbon cascades, navy, powder blue, ivory and gold ornaments and champagne berry picks in a woven tree collar" loading="lazy"></p><ol>\n<li><b>4 inch dusty blue velvet ribbon</b> tied into big bows and run in loose cascades.</li>\n<li><b>Blue and ivory floral ribbon</b> layered beside the velvet.</li>\n<li><b>Navy, powder blue, ivory and gold ornaments,</b> clustered in threes.</li>\n<li><b>Champagne berry picks</b> tucked in the gaps.</li></ol>\n<h2>Formula 3: Ribbon as the garland</h2><p><img src="/images/christmas-tree-ribbon-garland.jpg" alt="Christmas tree wrapped in camel velvet and champagne ribbon swags with a woven tree collar" loading="lazy"></p><ol>\n<li><b>Camel velvet wired ribbon</b> wrapped in loose horizontal swags.</li>\n<li><b>Champagne metallic wired ribbon</b> layered between the velvet.</li>\n<li><b>A few champagne ornaments</b> only. The ribbon is the star.</li></ol>\n<h2>The rules for all three</h2><ul><li>Lights first, ribbon second, ornaments last.</li><li>Plan about 10 yards of ribbon for a 7.5 ft tree.</li><li>Finish with the <b>woven tree collar</b> so the base looks as good as the top.</li></ul>\n<p>Tree still looks flat? Read <a href="/guides/designer-christmas-tree/">Why Does Your Tree Look Flat?</a> and <a href="/guides/tree-base-styling/">tree base styling</a>.</p>', ['B0GV2VFV62', 'B09337KL6W', 'B0FP1CFZTK', 'B0FJ1XZ48D', 'B0D2Z9SFT8', 'B0DG2VR3WL', 'B08D69PHQT', 'B0D1G162HV', 'B09VGDW1YZ', 'B0H8J573ZN'], None),
('christmas-table-decor-ideas', 'Christmas Table Decor Ideas', 'Holiday', 'christmas', 'img:christmas-table-decor-ideas', 'Woven placemats, tartan napkins, tree plates and a cedar garland down the middle.', '<p>A Christmas table looks collected when it mixes one pattern, one texture and one classic dish. Tartan is the pattern, woven placemats are the texture, and tree plates are the classic.</p>\n<h2>The 6 pieces, in order</h2><ol>\n<li><b>Round woven placemats.</b> Natural texture under every plate keeps the red and green from feeling loud.</li>\n<li><b>Christmas tree dinner plates with green trim.</b> The one piece everyone recognizes.</li>\n<li><b>Tartan plaid cotton napkins</b> folded flat on each plate. A 12 pack covers a full table plus spares.</li>\n<li><b>A real touch cedar garland</b> down the center as the runner.</li>\n<li><b>Brass taper holders</b> along the garland.</li>\n<li><b>White taper candles.</b> Unscented at the table, always.</li></ol>\n<h2>The styling rules</h2><ul><li>Keep the centerpiece under 14 inches so guests can see each other.</li><li>One pattern only. If the napkins are tartan, everything else is solid.</li><li>Set it the night before so the day of is easy.</li></ul>\n<p>Hosting breakfast too? See <a href="/guides/christmas-morning-table/">Christmas Morning: Set It the Night Before</a>.</p>', ['B08ZN6FYWN', 'B0B7W8XZYD', 'B09F2Z6PLX', 'B0H9RWQ9WK', 'B07W554ZNB', 'B07DWH5J2S'], None),
('gift-wrapping-ideas-that-look-expensive', 'Gift Wrapping Ideas That Look Expensive (Plus Gifts Under $50)', 'Holiday', 'christmas', 'img:gift-wrapping-ideas-that-look-expensive', 'Plain kraft paper, velvet ribbon, a blank tag and a dried orange. Then four gifts under $50 to put inside.', '<p>Expensive looking gifts are not about fancy paper. They are about one plain paper, one rich ribbon and one natural detail, repeated on every gift so the pile under the tree looks planned.</p>\n<h2>The wrapping kit</h2><ol>\n<li><b>Brown kraft paper,</b> 36 inch roll. Wide enough for boxes, and one roll lasts all season.</li>\n<li><b>Burgundy velvet ribbon.</b> Velvet is what reads expensive.</li>\n<li><b>Dark green velvet ribbon</b> for every other gift.</li>\n<li><b>Plain kraft tags</b> on twine. Write names in black pen.</li>\n<li><b>Dried orange slices</b> tucked into the bow.</li></ol>\n<h2>Gifts under $50 that fit the look</h2><ol>\n<li><b>WoodWick vanilla sea salt candle.</b> The crackling wick is the gift.</li>\n<li><b>Cotton cable knit throw.</b> Works for anyone with a couch.</li>\n<li><b>Scalloped marble cheese board.</b> Looks far more than it costs.</li>\n<li><b>White footed pedestal bowl.</b> A host or new homeowner favorite.</li></ol>\n<h2>The rules</h2><ul><li>Same paper on every gift, alternate the ribbon colors.</li><li>Wrap the ribbon both ways and tie the bow on top, off center.</li><li>Cut ribbon ends at an angle so they do not fray.</li></ul>\n<p>Bringing something to a party? See <a href="/guides/hostess-gift-ideas-christmas/">Christmas hostess gift ideas</a>.</p>', ['B07KKP6D3Z', 'B0FH4XMG94', 'B0FH4Z8PHN', 'B01767EKXC', 'B0F5MJHCNX', 'B078NXXHKX', 'B0B38YC8CK', 'B0DC6XJG1G', 'B0DLKKZDB1'], None),
('hostess-gift-ideas-christmas', 'Christmas Hostess Gift Ideas for the Hostess Who Has Everything', 'Holiday', 'christmas', 'img:hostess-gift-ideas-christmas', 'She said she has everything covered. Bring something she will use that night or keep for years.', '<p>You asked what to bring and she said she has everything covered. You still do not want to show up empty handed. The best hostess gifts do one of two things: help her clean up after the party, or become part of her Christmas every year after.</p>\n<h2>Things she will use that night</h2><ol>\n<li><b>Embroidered Christmas cloth napkins,</b> set of 4. Tie with a ribbon and hand them over.</li>\n<li><b>Linen hemstitch cocktail napkins,</b> 12 pieces. Perfect for the drinks table.</li>\n<li><b>A white marble wine cooler.</b> Bring it with a bottle inside and it is a two-in-one gift.</li>\n<li><b>GEOMETRY Christmas wreath tea towels,</b> set of 4. Quick dry, so they actually get used.</li></ol>\n<h2>Things she will keep for years</h2><ol>\n<li><b>Spode Christmas Tree trivet.</b> The classic pattern she may already collect.</li>\n<li><b>Spode Christmas Tree 3-piece serving set.</b> Serving fork, spoon and slotted spoon.</li>\n<li><b>Lenox 2026 annual ornament.</b> Dated, so it marks the year of the party.</li>\n<li><b>Lenox cardinal ornament.</b> A meaningful one for anyone who has lost someone.</li>\n<li><b>Lenox Santa fire truck ornament.</b> For the hostess with kids or a firefighter in the family.</li>\n<li><b>Lenox snow globe tree ornament.</b> The safest pick if you do not know her style.</li></ol>\n<h2>How to give it</h2><ul><li>Hand it to her with a quiet "this is for you, not for tonight" so she does not feel she has to use it right away.</li><li>Put a tag on it with your name. Hosts get a lot of gifts in one night.</li><li>Under $50 is the sweet spot for a hostess gift.</li></ul>\n<h2>Hostess gifts under $30 that look expensive</h2><p>On a budget? These look like they came from a kitchen boutique. Most are under $30, so you can pair two.</p><ol>\n<li><b>A 14 inch olive wood cheese board.</b> Every piece has its own grain, so it feels one of a kind.</li>\n<li><b>A marble and wood appetizer board with a knife.</b> Ready to use the night of the party.</li>\n<li><b>A marble and gold cheese knife set.</b> Tuck it under the ribbon on the cheese board for a two-part gift.</li>\n<li><b>An amber glass scented candle.</b> The hobnail jar looks far pricier than it is.</li>\n<li><b>A glass olive oil bottle.</b> Fill it with good olive oil and tie on a tag.</li>\n<li><b>A textured ceramic vase.</b> Bring it with a few stems of eucalyptus or pine.</li>\n<li><b>Acacia salad servers.</b> Warm wood that goes with every kind of dinnerware.</li></ol>\n<p>Want it to look beautiful too? See <a href="/guides/gift-wrapping-ideas-that-look-expensive/">gift wrapping ideas that look expensive</a>.</p>', ['B0H98Z2R1J', 'B0H14TXQ8V', 'B001J85V24', 'B0HJFG6NZT', 'B071S8NQZP', 'B003KKLWVS', 'B0GM535C8G', 'B0BSR3HCG7', 'B0CTXYX4HK', 'B0CTXZJMCR', 'B001GI7QZC', 'B07DM95RGT', 'B09X9H4H5Z', 'B099N339G7', 'B0821Y5BS3', 'B0DYNNJWG1', 'B07M5X6X3F'], None),
]
